              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked what relief would be available if a federal penal institution denied religious practices protected by RFRA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "319289d27b2a0a54aee18a0abff80cc3bd196d66f744fd59b3c04fd1183980c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-319289d27b2a-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg raised the practical problem of states releasing or transferring prisoners to avoid liability, suggesting that damages might be necessary to ensure compliance."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "319289d27b2a0a54aee18a0abff80cc3bd196d66f744fd59b3c04fd1183980c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-319289d27b2a-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned the inducement for prisons to comply, noting allegations that some wait until the eve of trial after extensive discovery and harm before capitulating."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "319289d27b2a0a54aee18a0abff80cc3bd196d66f744fd59b3c04fd1183980c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-319289d27b2a-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer noted that some cases interpret \u201cappropriate relief\u201d to include damages while others do not."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "319289d27b2a0a54aee18a0abff80cc3bd196d66f744fd59b3c04fd1183980c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-319289d27b2a-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the Spending Clause creates a contract\u2011like protection that lessens the need for a strict construction of waivers of immunity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "319289d27b2a0a54aee18a0abff80cc3bd196d66f744fd59b3c04fd1183980c2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-319289d27b2a-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia referenced the case Barnes in asking whether the issue had been contested there."
      }
